IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 (Commonwealth of Australia), Part VA (tax file numbers) -- what the person starting a job
-- meets: who is a "recipient" (s 202A, s 202AA); applying for a tax file number and what the Commissioner must do with the
-- application (ss 202B, 202BA), a deemed refusal (s 202BC), interim notices to a payer (s 202BD); the TFN declaration to a
-- payer (s 202C), when it has effect and when it stops (s 202CA), quoting the TFN in it, the pending-application statement and
-- its 28 days (s 202CB), the payer sending it on (s 202CD), a wrong TFN (s 202CE(1)-(3), (6)), the payer's notice where no
-- declaration is made (s 202CF), the pension exemption (s 202EA(2)), and review in the Tribunal (s 202F(1)).
--
-- SEAT: the individual starting a job (Chloe at 15, Jake at 15 with no job yet, Daniel at 16). "Do I have to give my employer
-- my TFN? How do I get one? I have applied but do not have it yet: how long do I have? What happens if I do not quote it?"
-- Provisions addressed to the Commissioner or the payer are encoded as what they mean for that person: what the Commissioner
-- must do with my application, by when my payer must send on my declaration or tell the Commissioner I made none.
--
-- Edition: the compilation registered as C2026C00333 (Federal Register of Legislation, retrieved 22 September 2026), as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/C1936A00027.txt, Part VA at lines 11481-12100.
--
-- Read with the Taxation Administration Act 1953 baseline
-- (../../../taxation-administration-act-1953/encodings/baseline-2026-10/), which answers s 8C(2) (not quoting a TFN is not a
-- failure to give information), ss 8WA-8WB (who may ask for a TFN) and the PAYG withholding from my wages (Sch 1 s 12-35),
-- including that the amount withheld comes from the withholding schedules. Cross-folder IMPORT is not possible in the stable
-- l4, so nothing from it is restated here; NOTES.md names the link.
--
-- NOT ENCODED. Division 4 (investments, ss 202D-202DR), ss 202EB-202EH, Division 8 (ss 203, 204); the alienated personal
-- services limbs of "payer" and "recipient"; s 202BA(4) (issue without application); s 202BB, s 202BE, s 202BF beyond review;
-- s 202CA(3) (the Commissioner's determination is an input); s 202CB(5); s 202CB(6)-(8) and s 202CE(7)-(9) (declarations given
-- to Centrelink, a Secretary or the Repatriation Commission by a claimant) answer `not covered`; s 202CEA; s 202CF(2) (the 2000
-- transitional notice); s 202CG beyond s 202CF(1A); s 202FA.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written from the individual's seat with the 2026-10-18 defaults. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 Part VA -- tax file numbers`

§§ `Questions this encoding does not cover`

-- The stable l4 has no REFUSE. A question that can reach a gap answers with an `Answer`: either `answered` with the value,
-- or `not covered` with the reason.
DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 202CB(6)-(8), s 202CE(7)-(9)
    `a TFN declaration given as a claimant to Centrelink, the Student Assistance or Employment Secretary, the Veterans' Affairs Secretary or the Repatriation Commission is not encoded (s 202CB(6) to (8))`

GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH A TYPE
DECLARE `Answer` a IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `the answer` IS AN a
    `not covered` HAS `because`    IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `s 202A, s 202AA -- am I a recipient of this payer`

-- s 202A: "recipient means: (a) a person who receives an eligible PAYG payment (other than an alienated personal services
-- payment), or is likely to receive such a payment". "eligible PAYG payment means: (a) a payment from which an amount must be
-- withheld under Subdivision 12-B (other than section 12-55), Subdivision 12-C or Subdivision 12-D in Schedule 1 to the
-- Taxation Administration Act 1953". Salary or wages paid to an employee are withheld from under s 12-35, which is in
-- Subdivision 12-B (a borrowed term, asked as a fact; the TAA baseline answers it).
-- s 202AA: "(a) a requirement to withhold a nil amount is treated as a requirement to withhold an amount" and "(c)" section
-- 12-1 (the exceptions to withholding) is "to be disregarded". So a 15-year-old whose pay is too small for anything to be
-- withheld is still a recipient.
-- "child means a person who is less than 16 years of age" is defined in s 202A but used nowhere in Part VA (NOTES.md
-- finding 1): no age appears in any rule below.
GIVEN `I am paid, or am likely to be paid, salary or wages by this payer as an employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this payer pays me, or is likely to pay me, another payment from which tax must be withheld under Subdivision 12-B (not s 12-55), 12-C or 12-D` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `I am a recipient of this payer` IF
        `I am paid, or am likely to be paid, salary or wages by this payer as an employee`
    OR  `this payer pays me, or is likely to pay me, another payment from which tax must be withheld under Subdivision 12-B (not s 12-55), 12-C or 12-D`

@export Am I a "recipient" of this employer or payer under s 202A, so that I may make a TFN declaration to them?
GIVEN `I am, or will be, paid wages by them as their employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this employer pays you, or is likely to pay you, salary or wages as their employee (including casual work), even if no tax comes out because the pay is small
      `they pay me something else that tax must be withheld from` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they pay you, or are likely to pay you, another payment from which tax must be withheld under Subdivision 12-B (other than s 12-55), 12-C or 12-D of Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953 (for example director's fees, or a payment under a labour hire arrangement)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a recipient of this payer` IF
    `I am a recipient of this payer` `I am, or will be, paid wages by them as their employee` `they pay me something else that tax must be withheld from`

§§ `s 202C -- do I have to give my employer my TFN`

-- s 202C(1): "A person who is a recipient of a payer, or expects to become a recipient of a payer, may make a TFN
-- declaration in relation to the payer." "May": nothing in Part VA obliges a recipient to make one or to quote a TFN, and
-- Part VA has no penalty on the recipient. (TAA s 8C(2), in the TAA baseline: not quoting is not a failure to give
-- information. The cost of not quoting is the higher withholding under the TAA's withholding schedules, not deposited.)
DECLARE `Must I give this payer my TFN` IS ONE OF
    `no: I may make a TFN declaration to this payer, stating my TFN or that my application for one is pending, but Part VA does not require me to (s 202C(1))`
    `no: I am not, and do not expect to be, a recipient of this payer, so Part VA gives me no TFN declaration to make to them`

@export Do I have to give this employer or payer my tax file number?
GIVEN `I am, or will be, paid wages by them as their employee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this employer pays you, or is likely to pay you, salary or wages as their employee (including casual work)
      `they pay me something else that tax must be withheld from` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether they pay you, or are likely to pay you, another payment from which tax must be withheld under Subdivision 12-B (other than s 12-55), 12-C or 12-D of Schedule 1 to the Taxation Administration Act 1953
GIVETH A `Must I give this payer my TFN`
`Do I have to give this payer my TFN` MEANS
    IF `I am a recipient of this payer` `I am, or will be, paid wages by them as their employee` `they pay me something else that tax must be withheld from`
    THEN `no: I may make a TFN declaration to this payer, stating my TFN or that my application for one is pending, but Part VA does not require me to (s 202C(1))`
    ELSE `no: I am not, and do not expect to be, a recipient of this payer, so Part VA gives me no TFN declaration to make to them`

§§ `ss 202B, 202BA, 202BC, 202BD -- getting a tax file number`

-- s 202B(1): "A person may apply to the Commissioner for the issue of a tax file number." No age, residence or job is
-- required. (2): "in the approved form", which "may require ... documentary evidence of the applicant's identity".
-- s 202BA(1): "Subject to subsection (3), if ... the Commissioner is satisfied that the applicant's identity has been
-- established, the Commissioner shall issue a tax file number"; (2): if "not satisfied as to the applicant's true identity,
-- the Commissioner may refuse"; (3): if satisfied that "(a) the applicant already has a tax file number; or (b) a notice under
-- section 202BD in relation to the applicant is in force; the Commissioner shall refuse". (5): issue is by "written notice of
-- the number"; (6): refusal by written notice with reasons. The Commissioner's satisfaction is a judgment, asked as a fact.
DECLARE `What the Commissioner does with my TFN application` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner must issue me a tax file number, by written notice of the number (s 202BA(1), (5))`
    `the Commissioner may refuse it, because the Commissioner is not satisfied as to my true identity (s 202BA(2))`
    `the Commissioner must refuse it, because I already have a tax file number or an interim notice about me is in force (s 202BA(3))`

@export What must the Commissioner do with my application for a tax file number?
GIVEN `the Commissioner is satisfied that my identity has been established` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied, from your application and its proof of identity, that your identity has been established (the Commissioner's judgment)
      `the Commissioner is satisfied that I already have a tax file number` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner is satisfied that you already have a tax file number
      `an interim notice about me under s 202BD is in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an interim notice about you, given to one of your payers under s 202BD, is in force
GIVETH A `What the Commissioner does with my TFN application`
`What must the Commissioner do with my TFN application` MEANS
    IF     `the Commissioner is satisfied that I already have a tax file number`
        OR `an interim notice about me under s 202BD is in force`
    THEN `the Commissioner must refuse it, because I already have a tax file number or an interim notice about me is in force (s 202BA(3))`
    ELSE IF `the Commissioner is satisfied that my identity has been established`
         THEN `the Commissioner must issue me a tax file number, by written notice of the number (s 202BA(1), (5))`
         ELSE `the Commissioner may refuse it, because the Commissioner is not satisfied as to my true identity (s 202BA(2))`

-- s 202BC(1): "If the Commissioner has not decided an application for a tax file number within 28 days after the application
-- is made, the applicant may, at any time, give to the Commissioner written notice that the applicant wishes to treat the
-- application as having been refused." The 28 days run from the day after the application (the day it is made is not
-- counted), so the notice may be given from the 29th day after it. (2): not "at a particular time if at that time" a s 202BD
-- notice has been issued to each payer named in the application and each is in force. (3) and s 202F(1)(a): the deemed
-- refusal can then be taken to the Tribunal.
@export May I now give the Commissioner notice that I treat my TFN application as refused?
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your application for a tax file number
      `today` IS A DATE @desc The day on which you want to give the notice
      `the Commissioner has decided my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has issued you a TFN or refused your application
      `interim notices are in force to every payer I named in my application` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you named one or more payers in your application and an interim notice about you is in force, today, to each of them
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I treat my TFN application as refused` IF
        (NOT `the Commissioner has decided my application`)
    AND `today` GREATER THAN (`the day I applied` PLUS 28)
    AND (NOT `interim notices are in force to every payer I named in my application`)

-- s 202BD(1): where my application names a payer, the Commissioner "may give to the payer a notice ... in relation to the
-- applicant". (2): it "remains in force for the period of 28 days commencing on the day specified in the notice" (the first
-- day counts). While it is in force I am "taken to have stated" my TFN in my TFN declaration to that payer (s 202CB(4)).
@export What is the last day on which an interim notice to my employer, about my pending TFN application, is in force?
GIVEN `the day the notice says it starts` IS A DATE @desc The day specified in the s 202BD notice the Commissioner gave your payer
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day the interim notice is in force` MEANS `the day the notice says it starts` PLUS 27

-- s 202BD(6): where, while my application is pending, I notify the Commissioner in writing of a payer not named in it, "the
-- payer's name and address shall, at the end of the period of 7 days after the notification, be taken to have been stated on
-- the application".
@export At the end of which day is an employer I told the Commissioner about after applying taken to be named in my TFN application?
GIVEN `the day I notified the Commissioner of the payer` IS A DATE @desc The day you told the Commissioner in writing of a payer you had not named in your pending TFN application
GIVETH A DATE
`the day at whose end the payer is taken to be named` MEANS `the day I notified the Commissioner of the payer` PLUS 7

§§ `ss 202C, 202CB, 202CE, 202EA -- does my TFN declaration state my tax file number`

-- s 202C(2): "To be effective, the declaration must be made to the payer or the Commissioner, and must be made in the approved
-- form."
-- s 202CB(1): "a TFN declaration is not effective for the purposes of this Part unless the tax file number of the recipient is
-- stated in the declaration." (2): I am "taken to have stated" it if the declaration says "(a) that an application by the
-- recipient for a tax file number is pending; or (b) that the recipient has a tax file number but does not know what it is
-- and has asked the Commissioner to inform him or her of the number." (3): if I fail "to inform the payer of the recipient's
-- tax file number within 28 days after making the declaration", (2) does not apply "in respect of any time after the end of
-- the period of 28 days". So if I tell the payer within the 28 days, (3) never bites; if I do not, the statement stops working
-- after the 28th day, and a late number does not revive it (the payer may write a number on only before sending the
-- declaration on, s 202CD(4), which it must do within 14 days); I may make a new declaration (s 202CC). NOTES.md finding 4.
-- (4): taken to have stated it "while a notice under section 202BD given to the payer in relation to the recipient is in
-- force".
-- s 202CE(1), (2): if the Commissioner gives my payer notice of my correct TFN, the declaration is "regarded ... as having
-- always stated the recipient's tax file number". (3), (6): if the Commissioner instead notifies my payer that the number is
-- not mine and is not satisfied that I have one, "on and from the day on which [that] notice ... takes effect, the TFN
-- declaration concerned shall be taken not to state the tax file number".
-- s 202EA(2): a person "being paid a pension or benefit referred to in subsection (5)" (age pension, disability support
-- pension, carer payment, pension PP (single), special benefit, special needs pension, a VEA Part III pension, income support
-- supplement) is taken to have quoted the TFN in a TFN declaration if it says so.
GIVEN `the day I made it` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `it states my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it says my TFN application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it says I have a TFN I do not know and have asked the Commissioner for it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have told my payer my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I told my payer my TFN` IS A DATE
      `an interim notice to my payer about me is in force on the day asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am paid a pension listed in s 202EA(5) and it says so` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner has given my payer my correct TFN under s 202CE(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a s 202CE(3) notice that the number is not my TFN has taken effect by the day asked about` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`my declaration is taken to state my TFN` MEANS
    IF `the Commissioner has given my payer my correct TFN under s 202CE(1)`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE IF `a s 202CE(3) notice that the number is not my TFN has taken effect by the day asked about`
         THEN FALSE
         ELSE     `it states my TFN`
              OR  (    (`it says my TFN application is pending` OR `it says I have a TFN I do not know and have asked the Commissioner for it`)
                   AND (    `the day asked about` AT MOST (`the day I made it` PLUS 28)
                        OR  (`I have told my payer my TFN` AND `the day I told my payer my TFN` AT MOST (`the day I made it` PLUS 28))))
              OR  `an interim notice to my payer about me is in force on the day asked about`
              OR  `I am paid a pension listed in s 202EA(5) and it says so`

@export On a given day, is my TFN declaration to this employer effective, that is, taken to state my tax file number?
GIVEN `the day I made my TFN declaration` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your TFN declaration to this employer or payer
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `I made it to the payer or the Commissioner, on the approved form` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the declaration to your employer or payer, or to the Commissioner, on the approved TFN declaration form
      `I gave it as a claimant to Centrelink, a Secretary or the Repatriation Commission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave this declaration to Centrelink, the Student Assistance or Employment Secretary, the Veterans' Affairs Secretary or the Repatriation Commission as a claimant of a payment (not encoded)
      `my declaration states my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you wrote your tax file number on the declaration
      `my declaration says my TFN application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the declaration says that your application for a tax file number is pending
      `my declaration says I have a TFN I do not know and have asked the Commissioner for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the declaration says you have a tax file number but do not know it and have asked the Commissioner to tell you
      `I have told my employer my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since told this employer or payer your tax file number
      `the day I told my employer my TFN` IS A DATE @desc The day you told them your tax file number (ignored if you have not)
      `an interim notice to my employer about me is in force on that day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an interim notice about your pending application, given by the Commissioner to this employer under s 202BD, is in force on the day asked about
      `I am paid a listed pension and my declaration says so` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are being paid an age pension, disability support pension, carer payment, pension PP (single), special benefit, special needs pension, a Veterans' Entitlements Act Part III pension or income support supplement, and your declaration says so
      `the Commissioner has given my employer my correct TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Commissioner has given your employer written notice that the number in your declaration was wrong and of your correct tax file number (s 202CE(1))
      `a notice that the number is not my TFN has taken effect` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the day asked about, a notice from the Commissioner to your employer that the number in your declaration is not your tax file number has taken effect (s 202CE(3))
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` MEANS
    IF `I gave it as a claimant to Centrelink, a Secretary or the Repatriation Commission`
    THEN `not covered` `a TFN declaration given as a claimant to Centrelink, the Student Assistance or Employment Secretary, the Veterans' Affairs Secretary or the Repatriation Commission is not encoded (s 202CB(6) to (8))`
    ELSE `answered` (    `I made it to the payer or the Commissioner, on the approved form`
                     AND `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day I made my TFN declaration`
                     AND `my declaration is taken to state my TFN` `the day I made my TFN declaration` `the day asked about` `my declaration states my TFN` `my declaration says my TFN application is pending` `my declaration says I have a TFN I do not know and have asked the Commissioner for it` `I have told my employer my TFN` `the day I told my employer my TFN` `an interim notice to my employer about me is in force on that day` `I am paid a listed pension and my declaration says so` `the Commissioner has given my employer my correct TFN` `a notice that the number is not my TFN has taken effect`)

-- s 202CB(2), (3): the 28 days after making a declaration that says my application is pending (or that I have asked the
-- Commissioner for my number). The day of making is not counted.
@export I said in my TFN declaration that my application is pending: by what day must I tell my employer my TFN?
GIVEN `the day I made my TFN declaration` IS A DATE @desc The day you made the TFN declaration saying your application for a TFN is pending
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to tell my payer my TFN` MEANS `the day I made my TFN declaration` PLUS 28

§§ `s 202CA -- when my TFN declaration stops having effect`

-- s 202CA(1): "a TFN declaration commences to have effect when it is made." (1A): it "ceases to have effect when the
-- recipient makes another TFN declaration in relation to the payer." (1B): it ceases "12 months after it is made if no
-- eligible PAYG payment is made by the payer to the recipient during that 12 month period." (1C): after a payment, it ceases
-- at the end of "a period of 12 months [that] then elapses without any further eligible PAYG payment". (2), (3): it ceases at
-- the end of a day fixed by the Commissioner's legislative instrument (an input). The 12 months run to the same date a year on
-- (`add months` clamps 29 February to 28 February).
@export On a given day, is my TFN declaration to this employer still in effect?
GIVEN `the day I made my TFN declaration` IS A DATE @desc The day you made your TFN declaration to this employer or payer
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE @desc The day you are asking about
      `I have since made another TFN declaration to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, by the day asked about, you have made another TFN declaration to the same employer or payer
      `they have paid me since I made it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this employer or payer has paid you (a payment that tax must be withheld from, even a nil amount) since you made the declaration and on or before the day asked about
      `the last day they paid me` IS A DATE @desc The last day on or before the day asked about on which they paid you (ignored if they have not)
      `a Commissioner's determination has ended TFN declarations like mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a legislative instrument of the Commissioner under s 202CA(3) has ended all TFN declarations, or a class including yours, on or before the day asked about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` IF
        `the day asked about` AT LEAST `the day I made my TFN declaration`
    AND (NOT `I have since made another TFN declaration to them`)
    AND (NOT `a Commissioner's determination has ended TFN declarations like mine`)
    AND `the day asked about` AT MOST (`add months` `the start of the 12 months` 12)
    WHERE
        `the start of the 12 months` MEANS
            IF `they have paid me since I made it` AND `the last day they paid me` GREATER THAN `the day I made my TFN declaration`
            THEN `the last day they paid me`
            ELSE `the day I made my TFN declaration`

§§ `ss 202CD, 202CF -- what my employer must do with my declaration, or without one`

-- s 202CD(1): where I give my payer a TFN declaration, the payer "shall ... (b) within 14 days after the declaration is made,
-- send the original to the office of a Deputy Commissioner". Penalty (on the payer): 10 penalty units; also (5A).
@export By what day must my employer send my TFN declaration on to the Tax Office?
GIVEN `the day I made my TFN declaration` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave your TFN declaration to your employer or payer
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for my payer to send on my TFN declaration` MEANS `the day I made my TFN declaration` PLUS 14

-- s 202CF(1): a payer that "commences a relationship ... under which ... the payer will make (or will be likely to make)
-- eligible PAYG payments to a person (the recipient) ... must give notice to the Commissioner in the approved form, within 14
-- days after the commencement of the relationship, unless a TFN declaration made by the recipient to the payer is in effect at
-- the end of that 14 day period." (1A): not if my TFN "has been disclosed to the payer under section 202CG before the end of
-- that 14 day period". (3): a payer that fails is "liable to pay to the Commissioner a penalty of 10 penalty units".
-- "In effect" is read here as in effect under s 202CA and effective under s 202CB(1) (it states my TFN, or is taken to), since
-- s 202CB(1) says an unquoted declaration "is not effective for the purposes of this Part" (NOTES.md finding 5). A declaration
-- made by a new employee has had no 12 months to lapse in, so only its making and its quoting are asked here.
@export If I make no effective TFN declaration, by what day must my new employer tell the Commissioner?
GIVEN `the day my job with this employer began` IS A DATE @desc The day your employment (or other relationship under which they will pay you) with this employer or payer began
      `I made a TFN declaration to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have made a TFN declaration to this employer or payer, on the approved form
      `the day I made my TFN declaration` IS A DATE @desc The day you made it (ignored if you have not)
      `my declaration states my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you wrote your tax file number on the declaration
      `my declaration says my TFN application is pending` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the declaration says your application for a tax file number is pending, or that you have asked the Commissioner for a number you have but do not know
      `I have told my employer my TFN` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have since told this employer your tax file number
      `the day I told my employer my TFN` IS A DATE @desc The day you told them (ignored if you have not)
      `an interim notice to my employer was in force at the end of the 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an interim notice about your pending application, given by the Commissioner to this employer under s 202BD, was in force on the 14th day after your job began
      `the Commissioner disclosed my TFN to them in those 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Tax Office gave this employer your tax file number, from a declaration you made to the Commissioner, within 14 days after your job began
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` MEANS
    IF     `the Commissioner disclosed my TFN to them in those 14 days`
        OR (    `I made a TFN declaration to them`
            AND `the end of the 14 days` AT LEAST `the day I made my TFN declaration`
            AND `my declaration is taken to state my TFN` `the day I made my TFN declaration` `the end of the 14 days` `my declaration states my TFN` `my declaration says my TFN application is pending` FALSE `I have told my employer my TFN` `the day I told my employer my TFN` `an interim notice to my employer was in force at the end of the 14 days` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the end of the 14 days`
    WHERE
        `the end of the 14 days` MEANS `the day my job with this employer began` PLUS 14

§§ `s 202F -- review of a decision about my TFN`

-- s 202F(1): "Applications may be made to the Tribunal for review of ... (a) a decision refusing an application for the issue
-- of a tax file number under section 202BA (including a decision that is to be taken to have been made by virtue of section
-- 202BC); (b) a decision to cancel a tax file number under section 202BE; (c) a decision to give a notice under subsection
-- 202CE(3)". A withdrawal and reissue under s 202BF is not listed. (2): the Tribunal may order the Commissioner to issue a TFN
-- pending review of a refusal.
DECLARE `Decision about my TFN` IS ONE OF
    `the Commissioner refused my application for a tax file number, or I treated it as refused under s 202BC`
    `the Commissioner cancelled my tax file number as issued under an identity not my true identity`
    `the Commissioner told my employer that the number in my TFN declaration is not my tax file number`
    `the Commissioner withdrew my tax file number and issued me a new one`

@export May I apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of this decision about my tax file number?
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Decision about my TFN` @desc Which decision of the Commissioner about your tax file number you want reviewed
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I seek review of the decision about my TFN` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `the Commissioner withdrew my tax file number and issued me a new one` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
